# Test: IS-IS adjacency config surface (spec-isis-5 circuit + adjacency FSM).
#
# VALIDATES: spec-isis-5-adjacency -- the per-interface leaves that drive the
#            adjacency FSM and Hello sender (circuit-type, hello-interval,
#            hold-multiplier, priority, level) validate through the real
#            ze-isis-conf.yang schema, on both a point-to-point and a broadcast
#            circuit (User Story 1, AC-1/AC-3/AC-7). A hold-multiplier outside
#            the 1..255 range is rejected by the YANG range constraint before the
#            engine builds a circuit (boundary: hold-multiplier 0).
# PREVENTS:  a regression where the adjacency-driving leaves are not wired into
#            the schema (validate passes vacuously) or the hold-multiplier bound
#            is not enforced (a 0 multiplier would advertise an instantly-
#            expiring adjacency).
#
# Live adjacency formation (two nodes reaching Up via the LAN three-way / P2P
# RFC 5303 handshake, hold-timer teardown, `show isis neighbor` listing the
# neighbour) needs raw L2 (AF_PACKET) on a Linux veth and is proven by:
#   - the two-engine unit test TestISISAdjacencyUp (in-memory circuit, runs on
#     any host), and
#   - the QEMU integration test + the FRR interop scenario isis-p2p-frr owned by
#     spec-isis-13.
# This functional test exercises the config wiring only: config file -> YANG
# schema -> per-interface adjacency leaves.

# --- Invalid hold-multiplier (0) is rejected by the YANG range. --------------
stdin=isis-adj-bad-holdmult:terminator=EOF_BAD
isis {
	net 49.0001.0000.0000.0001.00
	interfaces {
		interface eth0 {
			hold-multiplier 0
		}
	}
}
EOF_BAD

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=isis-adj-bad-holdmult:exit=1
expect=exit:code=1

# --- Valid P2P + broadcast adjacency config validates. -----------------------
stdin=isis-adj-valid:terminator=EOF_VALID
isis {
	net 49.0001.0000.0000.0001.00
	level l1-l2
	interfaces {
		interface eth0 {
			circuit-type point-to-point
			hello-interval 3
			hold-multiplier 3
			level l1-l2
		}
		interface eth1 {
			circuit-type broadcast
			hello-interval 10
			hold-multiplier 10
			priority 64
			level l1
		}
	}
}
EOF_VALID

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=isis-adj-valid:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid
